From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBook <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: SystemUI: the pointer shake without a headless
 system user

ContextualCursorInteractor listens for the pointer shake (contextual
cursor, enable_contextual_cursor_desktop_entrypoints) only while the user
is set up, the device provisioned and entered, and "logged in", which it
reads as UserLogoutInteractor.isLogoutEnabled: a device-policy logout, or
config_userSwitchingMustGoThroughLoginScreen with a user that can log out.
The system user never can. On a device without a headless system user
(OpenBook: the person uses user 0), the shake was therefore never armed.

Treat the logout condition as met when there is no headless system user.
With one, nothing changes. The other three conditions stay.

The test that expects no shake without logout now runs only on a headless
system user device; a new test covers the other case.
---
 .../ContextualCursorInteractorTest.kt         | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../interactor/ContextualCursorInteractor.kt  |  9 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

